| --- | --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">入力検査</span><span lang="en">Input validation</span> | <span lang="ja">数量と通貨を独立に検査</span><span lang="en">Check quantity and currency independently</span> | <span lang="ja">検査済み値または集約した入力エラー</span><span lang="en">Validated values or accumulated input errors</span> |
| <span lang="ja">純粋計算</span><span lang="en">Pure calculation</span> | <span lang="ja">価格と規則から更新候補を計算</span><span lang="en">Calculate candidate from prices and rules</span> | <span lang="ja">妥当な候補または業務条件の不成立</span><span lang="en">Valid candidate or rejected business condition</span> |
| <span lang="ja">操作の解釈</span><span lang="en">Interpretation</span> | <span lang="ja">認可・Provider・競合条件を適用</span><span lang="en">Apply authorization, Provider and conflict checks</span> | <span lang="ja">操作の結果または実行時の失敗</span><span lang="en">Operation outcome or execution failure</span> |
| <span lang="ja">UoWの終了</span><span lang="en">UoW termination</span> | <span lang="ja">commit / abortと資源解放</span><span lang="en">Commit/abort and release resources</span> | <span lang="ja">確定を含む実行の結果</span><span lang="en">Execution outcome including commitment</span> |

# Verifying Models, Calculations and Execution Boundaries｜モデル・計算・実行の境界ごとに検証する

<span lang="ja">同じ規則を全体の結合試験だけで確認するのではなく、型、純粋計算、操作記述、実行境界に検証を分けます。どの段階で何を保証するかを明確にすると、変更時に確認すべき範囲も整理できます。</span><span lang="en">Verification is divided among types, pure calculations, operation descriptions and execution boundaries instead of relying solely on end-to-end tests. Explicit responsibilities also clarify what must be checked after a change.</span>

## Using Examples, Properties and Operation Records｜実例・性質・操作記録を使い分ける

<span lang="ja">純粋計算は、既知の入力と期待結果に加え、通貨を変えずに計算する、許されない数量を受け付けない、といった性質で検証できます。Consequenceの合成では、独立したエラーが失われないことと、失敗後に依存する処理へ進まないことを確認します。モナドなどの合成則と業務上の性質は、どちらも型検査だけで自動的に確認されるものではありません。</span><span lang="en">Pure calculations support known input/output examples and properties such as preserving currency or rejecting invalid quantities. Consequence composition is checked for error accumulation and skipped dependent work after failure. Neither algebraic composition laws nor business properties are automatically established by type checking alone.</span>

<span lang="ja">操作記述には、応答を与えるテスト用インタープリタや記録機構を使い、実際の通信を行わずに選ばれる操作を確認できます。CNCFの計画・記録契約も、与えた型付き応答に沿って訪れた操作を記録する範囲を定めています。実Providerによる認可、競合、commit・abort、資源解放は別の検証対象とし、記録機構の結果を本番実行の証明には置き換えません。</span><span lang="en">A test interpreter or recorder can supply responses and inspect selected operations without performing real communication. CNCF’s planning and recording contract likewise defines recording of visited operations under supplied typed responses. Real Provider authorization, conflicts, commit/abort and resource release need separate verification; a recorded simulation does not establish production behavior.</span>

#+CAPTION: <span lang="ja">確認したい性質と検証の境界</span><span lang="en">Properties and verification boundaries</span>
| <span lang="ja">確認したいこと</span><span lang="en">Question</span> | <span lang="ja">用いる確認</span><span lang="en">Verification</span> | <span lang="ja">分担する範囲</span><span lang="en">Scope</span> |
| --- | --- | --- |
| <span lang="ja">意味の異なる値を接続していないか</span><span lang="en">Are incompatible values connected?</span> | <span lang="ja">型検査</span><span lang="en">Type checking</span> | <span lang="ja">型に表した接続条件</span><span lang="en">Encoded connection conditions</span> |
| <span lang="ja">計算が業務規則を満たすか</span><span lang="en">Does calculation satisfy business rules?</span> | <span lang="ja">実例・性質の検査</span><span lang="en">Example and property tests</span> | <span lang="ja">固定した入力に対する出力</span><span lang="en">Outputs for fixed inputs</span> |
| <span lang="ja">失敗が適切に伝わるか</span><span lang="en">Does failure propagate correctly?</span> | <span lang="ja">合成の検査</span><span lang="en">Composition checks</span> | <span lang="ja">打切り・集約・結果の意味</span><span lang="en">Short-circuiting, accumulation, outcome meaning</span> |
| <span lang="ja">意図した操作を選ぶか</span><span lang="en">Are intended operations selected?</span> | <span lang="ja">テスト用解釈・操作記録</span><span lang="en">Test interpretation / recording</span> | <span lang="ja">与えた応答に対する経路</span><span lang="en">Paths under supplied responses</span> |
| <span lang="ja">実環境で正しく終了するか</span><span lang="en">Does real execution terminate correctly?</span> | <span lang="ja">Provider・結合検証</span><span lang="en">Provider and integration checks</span> | <span lang="ja">認可・競合・確定・資源解放</span><span lang="en">Authorization, conflicts, commit, cleanup</span> |

## Keeping AI Supplementation within Models and Shared Contracts｜AIによる補完をモデルと共通契約へ沿わせる

<span lang="ja">純粋関数型、モナド、Free Monadは、学習と手作業の記述に負担があります。AIに型と操作契約、既存の合成例を与えることで、この構造に沿う補完コードを作成しやすくなります。人間は業務の意味、失敗時の扱い、確定範囲を定め、型検査と境界ごとの検証で生成物を確認します。</span><span lang="en">Pure functional programming, monads and Free Monad require learning and manual effort. Supplying AI with types, operation contracts and established composition examples helps produce supplementary code within this structure. People define business meaning, failure handling and commit boundaries, while type checks and boundary-specific verification check the result.</span>

<span lang="ja">型は値と接続を、Consequenceは結果の扱いを、操作DSLとUoWは実装と実行の境界を限定します。既存の処理を再利用し、必要な補完とグルーコードをこの範囲へ置くことで、AIが独自の制御を作り込む範囲を減らせます。この組合せがプログラミング・ハーネスとしても機能し、修正とレビューをモデル上の意味に沿って進める助けになります。</span><span lang="en">Types constrain values and connections, Consequence standardizes outcomes, and the operation DSL with UoW bounds implementation and execution. Reuse and supplementary glue within these contracts reduce independently invented control logic. The combination also functions as a programming harness, keeping changes and reviews tied to model meaning.</span>

# Conclusion｜まとめ

<span lang="ja">型と純粋関数で業務モデルを計算へ具体化し、Consequenceで成功・失敗をつなぎ、Free Monadで操作を記述し、UoWの共通経路で実行します。この分担により、モデルの意味を保ちながら、業務計算とリアクティブな実行制御を組み合わせられます。AIによる補完にも同じ契約と検証を適用し、高度な手法を開発へ取り入れやすくします。</span><span lang="en">Types and pure functions turn business models into calculations; Consequence connects outcomes, Free Monad describes operations, and the shared UoW path executes them. This division combines business calculation with reactive execution controls while preserving model meaning. Applying the same contracts and verification to AI supplementation makes these advanced techniques more accessible in development.</span>

# Appendix: References and Implementation Mappings｜付録：参考文献と実装上の対応

<span lang="ja">2冊は、本書で用いるモデリング技術を整理する補助線です。F#やScala/Scalazの書籍中の実装をそのままTextus/CNCFの仕様とは扱いません。対応表に示す考え方を参照し、製品固有の型と実行契約はローカルの設計・実装を根拠に説明しています。</span><span lang="en">The two books provide reference perspectives for techniques used in this guide. Their F# and Scala/Scalaz implementations are not treated as Textus/CNCF specifications. The table relates their ideas to this guide; product-specific types and execution contracts are grounded in local designs and implementations.</span>

## The Two Books and Their Use in This Guide｜2冊の参考文献と本文の対応

<span lang="ja">Scott Wlaschin, Domain Modeling Made Functional: Tackle Software Complexity with Domain-Driven Design and F#（Pragmatic Bookshelf, 2018）。型による業務概念と制約の表現、関数としての処理の接続を参照します。https://pragprog.com/titles/swdddf/domain-modeling-made-functional/ 。公開抜粋：https://media.pragprog.com/titles/swdddf/modeling.pdf</span><span lang="en">Scott Wlaschin, Domain Modeling Made Functional: Tackle Software Complexity with Domain-Driven Design and F# (Pragmatic Bookshelf, 2018). Referenced for business concepts and constraints represented in types and connected as functions. https://pragprog.com/titles/swdddf/domain-modeling-made-functional/ . Public excerpt: https://media.pragprog.com/titles/swdddf/modeling.pdf</span>

<span lang="ja">Debasish Ghosh, Functional and Reactive Domain Modeling（Manning, 2016）。操作の契約と実装の分離、純粋な業務計算と作用の分離、リアクティブなモデルとの接続を参照します。https://www.manning.com/books/functional-and-reactive-domain-modeling 。公開目次：https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/functional-and-reactive/9781617292248/</span><span lang="en">Debasish Ghosh, Functional and Reactive Domain Modeling (Manning, 2016). Referenced for separating operation contracts from implementations, pure domain calculations from effects, and connections to reactive modeling. https://www.manning.com/books/functional-and-reactive-domain-modeling . Public contents: https://www.oreilly.com/library/view/functional-and-reactive/9781617292248/</span>

